    "created_at": "2015-12-04T06:21:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-12-04T06:21:20Z",
    "body": "This definitely helps. My only worry would be that given\n\n> It is the responsibility of specifications using Web IDL to state which global environment (or, by proxy, which global object) each platform object is associated with. \n\nHTML might not be doing this correctly. We could gloss over that, I guess, and leave the problem for another day. But there's a lot of \"create a new `Foo`\" throughout the spec, instead of \"create a new `Foo` associated with the current execution context's realm's global object\" (or alternately the entry/incumbent setting object's global object, or similar).\n\nIn any case, I think I will definitely proceed with the plan of eliminating \"JavaScript global environment\" using these definitions. Probably in the same commit that fixes #382.\n",
