    "created_at": "2015-12-04T06:32:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-12-04T06:32:49Z",
    "body": "> HTML might not be doing this correctly.\n\nIt probably isn't, in general.  That's why @annevk is trying to have IDL define the global environment association in more cases (and in practice I suspect it will end up being the global environment of the `this` value of the call for non-constructor things that do \"create a new `Foo`\").  But it's already defined for the one relevant case here: when an object is created via a constructor call.\n",
